    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0262" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg154"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Young.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister Baker reports that American steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Costa
                        Rica</hi>, on which he was a passenger, was fired upon at Amapala after
                    clearance because the captain refused, on demand, to give up Bonilla, a
                    Honduran, also a passenger. By direction of the President Mr. Young will protest
                    against this wanton and illegal act.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
